Novelty.strongest_argument:
I did not find a direct prior. The gate is refuted as a recombination whose closest ICL-specific instance is still uncited, so the novelty ledger overstates its delta and coverage is still incomplete (cap 74).

1. The proposal concedes the recombination itself ("Every component is published; the delta is their combination").

2. The decisive contrast is already published in KV compaction. A state confined to the context's own keys is set against a free state fitted by KL to the model's own context-conditioned outputs (Attention Matching vs Cartridges, 2602.16284 / 2506.06266 / 2609.17346).

3. The closest ICL-specific design was published on 2026-05-15 and appears nowhere in the package: "How Few-Shot Examples Add Up" (arXiv 2605.16591; Wang, Wang, Bakalova, Hahn). On six pretrained LMs (gemma-2 2B/9B/27B, Llama-3.2 1B/3B, Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct) it tests whether the n-shot ICL state lies in the span of the demonstrations' own per-example contributions. Its design elements line up with the gate's:
   - one weight vector shared across all prompts, fitted by global ridge OLS (the gate's shared map B);
   - per-example contributions built alone, by attention-edge ablation, and in context (the gate's alone vs in-context keys);
   - a "mismatched dictionary" null that swaps per-example components across prompts (the gate's resample placebo). This null keeps R^2 at about 0.70-0.80 against at least 0.875 for the real fit, which exposes a shared task-level part (the gate's family-constant floor);
   - the reconstructed state is injected into zero-shot prompts and scored on behaviour (the gate's student evaluation).
   Wave 1 retrieved this paper four times (KI-15, KI-20, AC-01, AC-04; KI-15 asked how low-rank the demonstration-induced change is). Nobody read it, and the D60 repair did not catch it.

4. Cartridges' keys stay near their initialisation. In "Learned Structure in Cartridges" (2508.17032, NeurIPS 2025 workshop), the free KV state is fitted by KL and its keys start from the context's own cache. They barely rotate during training, the learning happens in the values, and keys swap between tasks at a 4-7% loss. That is a published KV-analogue reading of the gate's own read-side question: the free state's read side stays at the context's own keys. The proposal screened it by title only ("none runs the comparison").

5. Han et al. (2305.12766, TMLR 09/2025) report on GPT-J that ICL attention and hidden features follow kernel regression over demonstrations, which is the representer (key-span) form. It is uncited.

6. Closest prior #5, Attention-Patching (OpenReview JHUthhdVQu), is the gate's S_free used as a method: per demonstration set, it fits layer-wise affine maps from non-contextual attention reads to the demonstration-induced change. It is still read from the abstract only, against rule 2.

What survives:
- the span constraint sits on the read side of a probe-dependent part, not the write side of a static function vector;
- a rank-matched free oracle under the same KL objective;
- per-episode framing with a label-prior floor;
- the identification controls I0-I7.

The first three are standard moves borrowed from these priors. The fourth is methodology rather than novelty. I am uncertain whether this amounts to a "trivial" recombination, and the lens says to default to refuted in that case.
